/* book exam traps: Reporting K > 1 as high conversion. K fixes only the equilibrium activity ratio; stoichiometry, feed, pressure and inerts also matter. | Using ΔG° sign for feasibility at the plant composition. Feasibility uses ΔG = RT ln(Q/K), not ΔG° alone. | Treating Q as if it were K. Q can be evaluated at any composition and it changes as the reaction proceeds; only at equilibrium does Q equal K. K is the fixed value of Q at equilibrium for the given temperature. | Confusing yield with selectivity. Yield is desired product per limiting reactant fed; selectivity is desired product per undesired product. | Forgetting pressure in gas activities. aᵢ = yᵢP/P° for an ideal gas; yᵢ alone is correct only when P = P° = 1 bar. */
